usage: gbdt_example.py [-h] --output-dir OUTPUT_DIR
                       [--bundle-path BUNDLE_PATH] [--input-dir INPUT_DIR]
                       {generate,run,verify-bundle}

Generate synthetic inputs and exercise a seeded B-to-B+C GBDT workflow.
Installed entry point: ``python -m aisimulate_core.sdk.gbdt_example``. These
formula targets are functional examples, never hardware measurements. No
downloaded data, model weights, external service, or GPU is used.

positional arguments:
  {generate,run,verify-bundle}

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --output-dir OUTPUT_DIR
                        A new directory; existing data is never replaced
  --bundle-path BUNDLE_PATH
                        verify-bundle only: override the packaged synthetic
                        manifest
  --input-dir INPUT_DIR
                        run only: externally managed directory from generate
